      "loss_weighting": {
        "note": "scripts/base_train.py computes the loss per micro-batch as the MEAN over that micro-batch's non-masked targets (nanochat.gpt, ignore_index=-1) and averages the grad_accum_steps micro-batch losses; a scored token therefore carries weight 1 / (active targets of its micro-batch * grad_accum_steps). Arms with different active counts in shared rows weight the SAME base tokens differently. This block measures that; nothing changes the objective (docs/EXPOSURE.md, 'Open experimental decision').",
        "note_distributed": "With world_size > 1 the per-micro-batch mean is taken WITHIN EACH RANK: rank r computes the mean over the non-masked targets of its own (B, T) device batch (rows [r*B, (r+1)*B) of the micro-batch's slice of the epoch order), divides by grad_accum_steps, and the distributed optimizer averages the gradients across ranks (nanochat.optim DistMuonAdamW, ReduceOp.AVG). A scored token on rank r therefore carries weight 1 / (active targets of rank r's micro-batch * grad_accum_steps * world_size). 'per_rank' and 'per_microbatch_rank_local' hold these rank-local denominators, the ones the current objective uses; 'per_microbatch' sums all B*world_size rows of a micro-batch and is the denominator only when world_size == 1.",
